85	
86	| # | Scenario | Expected |
87	|---|---|---|
88	| 1 | `readSavedMessageEntryIds()` with nothing ever written | `{}` |
89	| 2 | `writeSavedMessageEntryIds({'m1': 'e1'})` then `readSavedMessageEntryIds()` | `{'m1': 'e1'}` |
90	| 3 | `readSavedMessageEntryIds()` over corrupted/non-JSON stored data | `{}` (no throw) |
91	| 4 | `ChatRepositoryImpl.savedEntryIdFor('m1')` before any local-cache-loading call has ever run | `null` (the untouched initial `{}` — this is the expected pre-load state; `ChatBloc` never calls it in this state, see note above) |
92	| 5 | `listMessages(sessionId)` succeeds, then `savedEntryIdFor('m1')` where `'m1'` was previously recorded | returns the recorded `entryId`, confirming the local-cache load populated `_savedMessageEntryIds` as part of `_ensureLocalCacheLoaded()` |
93	| 6 | `recordMessageSaved(chatMessageId: 'm1', entryId: 'e1')` | `_localCache.writeSavedMessageEntryIds` is called with a map containing `{'m1': 'e1'}` merged with whatever was already in memory; a subsequent `savedEntryIdFor('m1')` returns `'e1'` without a new storage read |
94	| 7 | `recordMessageSaved` called twice for the same `chatMessageId` with the same `entryId` (simulating a retried save after a lost local record, research.md R1/FR-004) | Second call is a harmless overwrite — no error, map still has exactly one entry for that id |
